(
    id: "scn_m01_elk_creek",
    display_name: "Elk Creek: The Debt",
    briefing: [
        "1865. Quartermaster Elias Ward signed a false loss report for Silas Teague. He told himself it was one dishonest wagon in a war full of graves. The paper let Teague's Elk Creek Ring steal military payroll, homestead claims, and the names of every witness who objected.",
        "Josiah Freed objected. Teague's riders hanged him beside his own field. His sister Naomi spent two years finding the counter-book that connects the stolen land, the paid killers, and Elias's signature.",
        "The book is not sacred. It is evidence, Elias's confession, and a list of people Teague will murder if he learns they spoke. Destroy it and the Ring walks free. Carry it and every witness becomes a target.",
        "This morning Naomi's wagon was stopped at Elk Creek. The affidavits burned. Naomi survived. Teague's riders are circling back to finish the work and silence her.",
        "Hold the creek. Save Naomi. Recover the surviving evidence. Elias Ward does not get to run from what his signature began.",
    ],
    prebattle_dialogue: [
        (speaker: "Naomi Freed", text: "My brother died because you put your name beneath Teague's lie.", voice: Some("m01_01_naomi.wav")),
        (speaker: "Elias Ward", text: "Yes.", voice: Some("m01_02_elias.wav")),
        (speaker: "Naomi Freed", text: "Do not give me a one-word confession. Give me a reason not to leave you for those riders.", voice: Some("m01_03_naomi.wav")),
        (speaker: "Elias Ward", text: "The counter-book proves who Teague bought, who he robbed, and who he means to kill next. I cannot undo Josiah. I can stand between Teague and the living.", voice: Some("m01_04_elias.wav")),
        (speaker: "Naomi Freed", text: "Then survive long enough to testify. I did not drag the truth this far to bury it with you.", voice: Some("m01_05_naomi.wav")),
        (speaker: "Elias Ward", text: "Powderburn Company! Hold the creek. Naomi lives. Teague gets nothing else today.", voice: Some("m01_06_elias.wav")),
    ],
    battle_dialogue: [
        (id: "m01_move", trigger: "first_player_move", speaker: "Naomi Freed", text: "The creek stones are slick. Take the bank, not the water."),
        (id: "m01_shot", trigger: "first_player_shot", speaker: "Elias Ward", text: "Make the first report true. One shot, one fact."),
        (id: "m01_hit", trigger: "first_enemy_hit", speaker: "Naomi Freed", text: "They found us. Keep the wagon between us and them."),
        (id: "m01_down", trigger: "first_enemy_down", speaker: "Elias Ward", text: "One rider down. The counter-book stays with the living."),
    ],
    score: Some("dust_and_ashes.wav"),
    date: "1867-04-12",
